  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Median is the central value (or middle observation) of statistical data if it is arranged in ascending or descending order.</p><p>Thus, if there are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;observations (variates) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math> arranged in ascending or descending order, then</p><p>median&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;observation, if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is odd</p><p>and median&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mtext>&#160;th observation&#160;</mtext><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mtext>&#160;th observation&#160;</mtext></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, if&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is even.</p><p>Here we can see there are&nbsp;even number of terms,</p><p>So, median&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>Mean deviation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8721;</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>58</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, median&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
